  "result": "Reservations with expiry are in, and `npm test` passes: 174 tests, 0 failed. That includes 8 new tests in `test/reservations.test.js` covering the store and the API.\n\n- **`src/store.js`:**\n  - `reserve`, `getAvailable`, `confirm` and `release` are added.\n  - `removeItem` now checks against available stock instead of physical stock.\n  - Expiry reads the store's `clock` option only.\n- **`src/api.js`:** `GET /stock/:sku` now also returns `available`. I added `POST /reservations`, `POST /reservations/:id/confirm` and `DELETE /reservations/:id` with the status codes you listed.\n\nFour choices the spec left open:\n- **Ids:** reservation ids are sequential strings like `r1`, `r2`. They're unique within a store but easy to guess.\n- **Expired reservations:** they stay in memory after expiry, so confirming one keeps returning `RESERVATION_EXPIRED`. Nothing prunes them.\n- **`ttlMs`:** it isn't validated. A missing or non-numeric value gives a reservation that never counts as active, because the expiry comparison with `NaN` never holds.\n- **`confirm` return value:** the store's `confirm` returns `{sku, stock}`, and the API passes that straight through as the 200 body.",
